---
import handoffDark from "../assets/crops/handoff-card-dark.png";
import handoff from "../assets/crops/handoff-card.png";
import Section from "./Section.astro";
import Shot from "./Shot.astro";
import Video from "./Video.astro";
---

<Section id="desktop" eyebrow="Your cloud computer" title="Work on a desktop you can watch and take over.">
  <p slot="lede" class="mt-6 text-lede text-pretty text-muted-foreground">
    In your own deployment, each user has a Linux desktop VM. Its files stay between jobs. The agent runs code and uses
    apps on it. You can watch it work, take the desktop, and hand it back.
  </p>

  <!-- Two tiles of one shape, so the captions line up. -->
  <div class="mt-14 grid gap-x-8 gap-y-14 lg:grid-cols-2">
    <figure>
      <div class="frame aspect-[956/726]">
        <Video
          name="screen-control"
          dark="screen-control-dark"
          label="Control of the cloud computer's screen: a typed command prints a table, then Release"
          class="rounded-2xl"
        />
      </div>
      <figcaption class="mt-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-medium">Control and Release</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 max-w-[34rem] leading-relaxed text-pretty text-muted-foreground">
          The screen streams live to your device. Press Control to use the desktop yourself; the agent's desktop tool stays
          locked until you press Release.
        </p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>

    <figure>
      <!-- The card on paper at about its size in the app. -->
      <div class="frame grid aspect-[956/726] place-items-center p-6">
        <div class="w-full max-w-[360px] rounded-xl bg-background p-1">
          <Shot
            src={handoff}
            dark={handoffDark}
            alt="A handoff card: Sign in to the reports site, with Done and Cancel"
            widths={[360, 720]}
            sizes="360px"
          />
        </div>
      </div>
      <figcaption class="mt-6">
        <h3 class="text-lg font-medium">Handoffs</h3>
        <p class="mt-2 max-w-[34rem] leading-relaxed text-pretty text-muted-foreground">
          On a sign-in page, a code request or a captcha, the agent stops and hands you the screen. You sign in on your
          cloud computer, press Done, and the job goes on. The agent is told never to solve a captcha.
        </p>
      </figcaption>
    </figure>
  </div>
</Section>
